{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And now, my son.</b> This is according to the way of our Sages of blessed memory (Avot 2:10): and repent one day before your death — meaning, for a person is never guaranteed even a single day of life, and through this he will always be in repentance. Therefore she said <b>and now</b> etc. <b>arise, flee</b> etc. — meaning, and now, immediately, without delay; for even though Esav said only ״יִקְרְבוּ״ etc., it is possible that Yitzhak may die at that very hour and he will put his thought into action." "<b>Flee for yourself to Lavan.</b> For he will stand against Esav if he goes to kill you:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviation זִכְרוֹנָם לִבְרָכָה as 'our Sages of blessed memory' in context, since the citation is from Avot and references the Sages."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:07.056371150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}